required, and redistribution is capped at ten Design Files per location without
written permission. This repository is exactly at that cap; an eleventh imported
file needs permission.

### Keyswitch KiCad Library — MIT OR CC BY-SA 4.0

Files: the switch, hotswap and stabilizer models under
`3dmodels/Kiboar_MechSwitch.3dshapes/` (except the Scotto `*_CAD.step` set
above), `3dmodels/Kiboar_Cutout.3dshapes/` and
`3dmodels/Kiboar_Stabilizer.3dshapes/`, plus the footprints under
`footprints/Kiboar_MechSwitch.pretty/`, `footprints/Kiboar_Cutout.pretty/` and
`footprints/Kiboar_Stabilizer.pretty/` where present.

Evidence: these files are byte-identical to files in the upstream library —
verified with SHA-256 for `Choc_V1`, `MX_PCB`, `MX_Plate`, `Hotswap_MX`,
`Stabilizer_MX_2.00u` and `Stabilizer_MX_6.25u` — and the STEP headers name
`kicad StepUp` with paths under `Switch_Keyboard_*`.

Source: <https://github.com/kiswitch/keyswitch-kicad-library>.
Licence: dual MIT / CC BY-SA 4.0 (`LICENSE-MIT` and `LICENSE-CC-BY-SA`).

**Verdict: MIT-compatible** when attributed. Use the MIT option.

### KiCad official libraries — CC BY-SA 4.0 with exception

Not redistributed. Kiboar references the user's installed KiCad models through
`${KICAD10_3DMODEL_DIR}`, and no file in this repository has been identified as
a KiCad library file. The KiCad exception does not apply to redistributing
library collections, so any footprint later copied from KiCad would have to be
treated as CC BY-SA 4.0.

Source: <https://www.kicad.org/libraries/license/>.

### Manufacturer CAD

Many models and footprints name a component vendor (Alps, Würth, Molex, TE
Connectivity, Kailh, E-Switch…). These come from the manufacturer's CAD
downloads. Vendor terms commonly allow the model to be used in a design but do
not grant redistribution as a library. They were not verified vendor by vendor;
treat them as "used by permission for design work" until each vendor's terms
are checked.

## Files with no recorded provenance

For most of the remaining models the `FILE_NAME` author field holds a CAD tool
name (`Author`, `SwSTEP 2.0`, `kicad StepUp`, `ST-DEVELOPER …`, `Unknown`), so
the origin cannot be established from the repository. Symbols without a
`SnapEDA_Link` and footprints without an in-file reference are in the same
position.

Those files are listed as **unknown**, not assumed MIT-clean. They cannot be
relicensed until their source is known.

